# Topic rights per account; anything not granted is refused. Each service publishes exactly
# its own contract topics (the topic table in docs/architecture/overview.md) and reads only
# what it uses. A read right must cover the subscription filter the service sends, so the
# three wildcard filters still in code (alert-manager `alerts/#`, historian and opcua-server
# `sensors/#`, historian `status/+`) keep wildcard read rights until those subscriptions
# name their topics.

user physics-engine
topic write sensors/plant
topic write sensors/boiler
topic write sensors/turbine
topic write sensors/system/heartbeat
topic write status/physics-engine

user plc-controller
topic write alerts/warning
topic write alerts/critical
topic write alerts/snapshot
topic write plc/events
topic write status/plc-controller

user alert-manager
topic read alerts/#
topic write alarms/changes

user historian
topic read sensors/#
topic read alarms/changes
topic read plc/events
topic read status/+

user api-gateway
topic read plc/events
topic read alarms/changes

user opcua-server
topic read sensors/#
topic read alarms/changes

# The container healthcheck reads the broker's own statistics.
user monitor
topic read $SYS/#
